   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to remedial\nprogram requirements",
    "basePrintNo": "S7225",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7225-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 56,
       "fullName": "Jeremy Cooney",
       "imgName": "1318_Jeremy_Cooney.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1501,
       "sessionMemberId": 1857,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "COONEY"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §27-1415, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7225\n\nSPONSOR: SALAZAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to reme-\ndial program requirements\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to ensure that remedial programs include\nconsideration of nearby school or day care facilities.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would clarify that the provisions of Environmental Conserva-\ntion Law § 27-1415, which relates to the development of remedial\nprograms for the Brownfield Cleanup Program.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Brownfield Cleanup Program recognizes the special status of schools\nand day care facilities by requiring proposal notification.  This legis-\nlation simply extends that recognition to ensure that when remedial\nprograms are being selected for a site, proximity to schools and day\ncare facilities is considered, in addition to the existing consideration\nof proximity to commercial, industrial, agricultural and recreational\nareas.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-2020: A10747(Niou) - referred to environmental conservation\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect March 1, 2022, and apply to all applications\nreceived on or after such date.\n",
